(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"14e05e03-dc83-4e5a-8a3f-8acf6b35572f"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"c0afa67b-adc2-4ee7-81f1-8019f660de2f"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"377e96fc-8b10-47b9-acdb-6686882ca5b0"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b4b6eb97-362f-4927-b5e9-fd5ffbb82264"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ccc35b3e-68b4-4258-95f4-86b9094e4165"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"199dd7c9-78ee-4102-93eb-84b074140c3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"78a2bcb3-cbdc-4fa1-b9cc-2b7d9a35be68"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bb901e81-46ab-4d8e-a164-66c0fed5e84d"],

Cell["\<\
The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette also \
sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output matches the \
screen.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fe07573b-102f-4be3-a952-a0a549c194ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c7d438c3-b890-493f-ad38-d538b4b999f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"69d5295d-df6e-4b9f-8450-8bdd76bf03d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"56128d8c-e9ff-4ea5-9e0d-14bc8a538e87"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a32b2fa2-85a5-41ab-b4a7-048a218f902a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c5f509ec-bc02-4da4-a9b0-6c0960356380"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"85fd3e87-bcde-440b-a891-3ea1d689a915"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2729429d-8155-41fc-a991-417dbfbeec19"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tag cell",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " names a cell, and ",
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inserts a red bracketed link to that name \[LongDash] the two together \
give a bibliography: style each entry ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tag it, cite it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"be0df5c2-1fe6-4634-817e-542bcb0261ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"adeec94e-0a6c-4914-b760-d539119a1ba6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"331d77df-474f-4722-99ad-2cd6a9b3873d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a bibliography tagged before that was true \[LongDash] or tagged \
through the Cell Tags dialog rather than the palette \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " labels every entry of a notebook at once, and clears the label of an entry \
whose tag you removed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"07f3564e-ea91-4a70-8d63-ccf1ca2d2566"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Existing tags are listed under ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8e4368a4-90ea-4780-8a37-367e167a0e83"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"281b6292-6ee4-4d2e-9b69-a61291ce9f01"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"e58c3130-a97c-4354-b2d7-d873e1cdedd4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"bf26590d-5993-\
444c-b69a-fc68d9e1723e"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1aabf2b2-6c3d-4bcd-be2e-77b5f3605c2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fc443a18-89e7-4de3-8266-b83402d4da81"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0ee29840-e304-446c-ba8a-e43fe2d2a523"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"96f118a8-45c1-4466-b7d5-32cf6289f3cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f616dbd1-ced0-461e-a639-e0ca3649cd0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e5d4264b-2091-475f-aa2a-5fd44c440b3d"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"55231218-3b88-416c-81ca-103a09b4f418"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"53277f4d-a360-40ee-a2a4-e5ab37a65bbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3c1a58df-d174-4d4f-a5a3-8056849aeaf4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the rest of the prose with it \[LongDash] the title, the \
headings, the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography \
entries, and both kinds of list \[LongDash] so the document keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b710b793-5741-4e56-ac78-f31ff7b13747"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bdef10b1-20b8-40f4-a535-f733d9d4db55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d73df605-3a84-43e6-9229-33748b94369c"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8f1060c6-7494-46bc-9339-ecd711d69d08"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"54ac6a12-bc91-4f46-8f1f-b3748478e392"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"08f7f2fc-6743-4fbf-809f-db5d56af2251"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"64b3caed-415e-4065-9609-f7dc4b773fba"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7bbf6c91-1ab7-4060-99e5-49cc44392283"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b568a3fe-110d-491e-a7a8-bad75d5ecfab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0f81db59-e791-4f08-ab13-c4e66139d025"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"726dd9b5-76b2-4fbf-8335-3ad7eab6f7b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"78d35859-863b-4de0-b61d-d7e7f08d1b5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"374320c5-03c7-4cc1-b61d-5e50329cde64"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a6882b27-1b53-42cd-88c2-b57b6b89168c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f84db38d-8ddd-4261-966f-953f3b1e0a90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"31132d08-e5c6-4710-a5ce-70dea8e4f7e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1b62c551-e661-4019-af22-4f2d30a04c76"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"760ff1f2-176f-4650-aaab-6e481fd95623"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"40eb4f57-4112-4224-a8aa-91fb013da92d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"09b77cb7-2a64-4647-9b5b-06a83f22b104"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"db27b4b9-dfe2-47f8-b1e4-3a3ceccd732b"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"45c18683-cdff-4924-96d1-47a7b808d2a6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select the cells to convert, then press ",
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". With nothing selected the whole notebook is converted."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e59e6b63-545a-4fdd-bfb6-999046685c05"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c52f93d6-9263-4973-adcd-084aff9c5381"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"42b3f904-40e1-43bb-a193-859912fa623c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6ae32c70-e79c-4dfb-9ca1-a31b3ccb5e5d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] TeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ade41511-42ac-487a-8bb7-b0f1fe348fdb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe. To bring in a LaTeX paper, paste it as Text cells and \
convert."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"085ce9e8-8ca3-4647-9908-3679af58bfee"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"951fbebb-6940-4924-9e96-92038b7dccbe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the MaTeX buttons; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do \
not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cb880ce1-8b81-439c-950f-99b151d3071f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"60be5872-e2f6-4880-a22a-a830a9c8bdee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f3a47a76-1c54-42aa-99b6-c7218238c359"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " renders the selected display equations through LaTeX; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " restores editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ae13e16f-5f1c-4372-a234-a4e2ffe63c1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1769223e-7ffe-4267-9387-71a3aa5c60f4"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f655e541-57ec-4e7a-b5b9-40dd750ac494"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3a31c208-aeb3-4fdd-ba67-2fa22a5265b6"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c4277b8c-d353-4699-b634-1403f764de0a"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ba15323b-0a55-4f59-b24c-439f3672702e"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"955425ad-1556-4785-a57d-63a34aa41e2b"],

Cell["\<\
Convert to LaTeX at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the \
notebook is the source.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dfaf56e0-718d-4bfb-a0a2-446ee20eb5a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and convert MaTeX cells back to math so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f1a31e13-feef-4200-81e0-fee742a9faae"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c867db01-0c1c-433a-ba65-0aac0a3dccb0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
